{:edb/db-before-t 1327 :edb/db-after-t 1328 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534640 50 #inst "2026-10-08T03:03:53.718Z" 13194139534640 true] [17592186184010 1100 "Find the solution of $2x^2-6 \\le -4x$." 13194139534640 false] [17592186184010 1100 "Find the solution of $2x^2-6 \\le -4x.$" 13194139534640 true] [17592186184010 1145 "To solve this inequality using the graphical method, we first need to move all of the numbers to the left-hand side so that the right-hand side is $0$.\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}2x^{2} - 6 & \\le - 4x \\\\ 2x^{2} + 4x - 6 & \\le 0 \\\\ x^{2} + 2x - 3 & \\le 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nSo, we want to find the values of $x$ for which the parabola\n\n$$\ny=x^2+2x-3\n$$\n\nlies below the $x$-axis. Let's find the roots of the parabola by factoring:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nx^{2} + 2x - 3 &= 0 \\\\\n(x - 1)(x + 3) &= 0\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe see that the roots are $x=1$ and $x=-3$, and we can graph the parabola as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/3833/Source/Images/4927c4ddb9348af5ed197223c5719193.png)\n\nSince we are interested in solving\n\n$$\nx^2+2x-3 \\le 0\n$$\n\nwe look for the part of the parabola that is below the $x$-axis.\n\nBased on the graph, the solution is\n\n$$\n-3 \\le x \\le 1\n$$\n\nUsing interval notation, we write $x \\in [-3,1]$." 13194139534640 false] [17592186184010 1145 "To solve this inequality using the graphical method, we first need to move all of the numbers to the left-hand side so that the right-hand side is $0.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{x}^{2}-6 & \\le -4x \\\\ 2{x}^{2}+4x-6 & \\le 0 \\\\ {x}^{2}+2x-3 & \\le 0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we want to find the values of $x$ for which the parabola $y=x^2+2x-3$ lies below the $x$-axis. Let's find the roots of the parabola by factoring:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+2x-3 & =0 \\\\ (x-1)(x+3) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe see that the roots are $x=1$ and $x=-3,$ and we can graph the parabola as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004892/assets/0fe5ab0d38cea340e2227157bf1d434a0fccbab153289db52106857530fbc4dc.png)\n\nSince we are interested in solving\n\n$$\nx^2+2x-3 \\le 0,\n$$\n\nwe look for the part of the parabola that is below the $x$-axis.  \n\nBased on the graph, the solution is $-3 \\le x \\le 1.$  \n\nUsing interval notation, we write $x \\in [-3,1].$" 13194139534640 true] [17592186184012 1100 "Find the solution of $x^2-2x-8 \\geq 0$." 13194139534640 false] [17592186184012 1100 "Find the solution of $x^2-2x-8 \\geq 0.$" 13194139534640 true] [17592186184012 1145 "To solve the inequality\n\n$$\nx^2-2x-8 \\geq 0\n$$\n\nwe need to find the values of $x$ for which the parabola\n$y=x^2-2x-8$\nlies *above* the $x$-axis or touches this axis.\n\nFirst, let's find the roots of the parabola:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nx^{2} - 2x - 8 &= 0 \\\\\n(x + 2)(x - 4) &= 0\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the roots are $x=-2$ and $x=4$, and we can graph the parabola as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/3833/Source/Images/d48ff6ef1caea411bdbfb5e32821a420.png)\n\nThe values marked in blue show all $x$-values where the parabola lies *above* the axis or touches this axis.\n\nSo, the solution to the inequality is\n\n$$\nx \\leq -2\n$$\n\nor\n\n$$\nx \\geq 4\n$$" 13194139534640 false] [17592186184012 1145 "To solve the inequality \n\n$$\nx^2-2x-8 \\geq 0,\n$$\n\nwe need to find the values of $x$ for which the parabola \n\n$$\ny=x^2-2x-8\n$$\n\nlies *above* the $x$-axis or touches this axis.\n\nFirst, let's find the roots of the parabola:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}-2x-8 & =0 \\\\ (x+2)(x-4) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the roots are $x=-2$ and $x=4,$ and we can graph the parabola as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004892/assets/6e9eeff6caaad8efe92d4726c1f04175ed3023ea99b7990436597233ef2910df.png)\n\nThe values marked in blue show all $x$-values where the parabola lies *above* the axis or touches this axis. \n\nSo, the solution to the inequality is $x \\leq -2$ or $x \\geq 4.$" 13194139534640 true] [17592186184061 1100 "Find the solution of $2x^2 < -4x$." 13194139534640 false] [17592186184061 1100 "Find the solution of $2x^2 < -4x.$" 13194139534640 true] [17592186184061 1145 "To solve this inequality using the graphical method, we first need to move all of the numbers to the left-hand side so that the right-hand side is $0$.\n$\\begin{bmatrix}2x^{2} & < - 4x \\\\ 2x^{2} + 4x & < 0\\end{bmatrix}$.\n\nSo, we want to find the values of $x$ for which the parabola\n\n$$\ny = 2x^2 + 4x\n$$\n\nlies below the $x$-axis. Let's find the roots of the parabola by factoring:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n2x^{2} + 4x &= 0 \\\\\n2x(x + 2) &= 0\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe see that the roots are $x = -2$ and $x = 0$, and we can graph the parabola as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/3833/Source/Images/bddb58670bbcb57b9f310b467227d839.png)\n\nSince we are interested in solving\n$2x^2 + 4x \\lt 0$,\nwe look for the part of the parabola that is below the $x$-axis.\n\nBased on the graph, the solution is $-2 < x < 0$.\n\nUsing interval notation, we write\n\n$$\nx \\in \\left(-2, 0\\right)\n$$" 13194139534640 false] [17592186184061 1145 "To solve this inequality using the graphical method, we first need to move all of the numbers to the left-hand side so that the right-hand side is $0.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{x}^{2} & <-4x \\\\ 2{x}^{2}+4x & <0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we want to find the values of $x$ for which the parabola $y = 2x^2 + 4x$ lies below the $x$-axis. Let's find the roots of the parabola by factoring:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{x}^{2}+4x & =0 \\\\ 2x(x+2) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe see that the roots are $x = -2$ and $x = 0,$ and we can graph the parabola as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004892/assets/936653d6efd2ff155768730d61af5b68924c48933fa81b77998a668b7691fa10.png)\n\nSince we are interested in solving \n\n$$\n2x^2 + 4x \\lt 0,\n$$\n\nwe look for the part of the parabola that is below the $x$-axis. \n\nBased on the graph, the solution is $-2 < x < 0.$ \n\nUsing interval notation, we write $x \\in \\left(-2, 0\\right).$" 13194139534640 true] [17592186184074 1100 "Find the solution of $-x^2 + 7 x - 10 \\leq 0$." 13194139534640 false] [17592186184074 1100 "Find the solution of $-x^2 + 7 x - 10 \\leq 0.$" 13194139534640 true] [17592186184074 1145 "To solve the inequality\n\n$$\n-x^2 + 7 x - 10 \\leq 0\n$$\n\nwe need to find the values of $x$ for which the parabola\n\n$$\ny = -x^2 + 7 x - 10\n$$\n\nlies *below* the $x$-axis or touches this axis.\n\nFirst, let's find the roots of the parabola:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-x^{2} + 7x - 10 &= 0 \\\\\n- (x^{2} - 7x + 10) &= 0 \\\\\n- (x - 2)(x - 5) &= 0\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the roots are $x=2$ and $x = 5$, and we can graph the parabola as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/3833/Source/Images/66589305706cca7f293953c16fb19690.png)\n\nThe values marked in blue show all $x$-values where the parabola lies *below* the $x$-axis or touches this axis.\n\nSo, the solution to the inequality is\n\n$$\nx \\leq 2\n$$\n\nor\n\n$$\nx \\geq 5\n$$" 13194139534640 false] [17592186184074 1145 "To solve the inequality \n\n$$\n-x^2 + 7 x - 10 \\leq 0,\n$$\n\nwe need to find the values of $x$ for which the parabola \n\n$$\ny = -x^2 + 7 x - 10\n$$\n\nlies *below* the $x$-axis or touches this axis.\n\nFirst, let's find the roots of the parabola:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-{x}^{2}+7x-10 & =0 \\\\ -({x}^{2}-7x+10) & =0 \\\\ -(x-2)(x-5) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the roots are $x=2$ and $x = 5,$ and we can graph the parabola as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004892/assets/13e108b6383e99c5840789389378fd58cd8704484296485cb6483112ecf4ae25.png)\n\nThe values marked in blue show all $x$-values where the parabola lies *below* the $x$-axis or touches this axis.\n\nSo, the solution to the inequality is $x \\leq 2$ or $x \\geq 5.$" 13194139534640 true] [17592186184276 1020 #edb/ref 17592186300503 13194139534640 true] [17592186184276 1020 #edb/ref 17592186300517 13194139534640 true] [17592186184276 1020 #edb/ref 17592186300524 13194139534640 true] [17592186184276 1020 #edb/ref 17592186300613 13194139534640 true] [17592186184277 1020 #edb/ref 17592186300510 13194139534640 true] [17592186184277 1020 #edb/ref 17592186300531 13194139534640 true] [17592186184277 1020 #edb/ref 17592186300538 13194139534640 true] [17592186184277 1020 #edb/ref 17592186300599 13194139534640 true] [17592186184277 1020 #edb/ref 17592186300606 13194139534640 true] [17592186184278 1020 #edb/ref 17592186300545 13194139534640 true] [17592186184278 1020 #edb/ref 17592186300571 13194139534640 true] [17592186184278 1020 #edb/ref 17592186300585 13194139534640 true] [17592186184278 1020 #edb/ref 17592186300592 13194139534640 true] [17592186184279 1020 #edb/ref 17592186300496 13194139534640 true] [17592186184279 1020 #edb/ref 17592186300552 13194139534640 true] [17592186184279 1020 #edb/ref 17592186300560 13194139534640 true] [17592186184279 1020 #edb/ref 17592186300565 13194139534640 true] [17592186184279 1020 #edb/ref 17592186300578 13194139534640 true] [17592186184710 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139534640 true] [17592186184710 1100 "Find the solution of $2x^{2} - 12 \\le - 5x$." 13194139534640 false] [17592186184710 1100 "Find the solution of $2{x}^{2}-12\\le -5x.$" 13194139534640 true] [17592186184710 1145 "To solve this inequality using the graphical method, we first need to move all of the numbers to the left-hand side so that the right-hand side is $0.$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{x}^{2}-12 & \\le -5x \\\\ 2{x}^{2}+5x-12 & \\le 0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we want to find the values of $x$ for which the parabola $y=2{x}^{2}+5x-12$ lies below the $x$-axis or touches this axis. Let's find the roots of the parabola by factoring:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{x}^{2}+5x-12 & =0 \\\\ (2{x}^{2}+8x)+(-3x-12) & =0 \\\\ 2x(x+4)-3(x+4) & =0 \\\\ (2x-3)(x+4) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe see that the roots are $x=-4$ and $x=\\frac{3}{2},$ and we can graph the parabola as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004892/assets/ba6c384800a5b42f2033527997328aa9f9d792b33b3fabecfe9b3a93789f46c4.png)\n\nSince we are interested in solving\n \n\n$$\n2{x}^{2}+5x-12\\le 0,\n$$\n\n we look for the part of the parabola that is below the $x$-axis or touches this axis.\n\n Based on the graph, the solution is $-4\\le x\\le \\frac{3}{2}.$ \n\nUsing interval notation, we write $x\\in [-4,\\frac{3}{2}].$" 13194139534640 true] [17592186184777 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534640 true] [17592186184777 1100 "Find the solution of $-x^{2} + 3x \\ge 0$." 13194139534640 false] [17592186184777 1100 "Find the solution of $-{x}^{2}+3x\\ge 0.$" 13194139534640 true] [17592186184777 1145 "To solve the inequality \n\n$$\n-{x}^{2}+3x\\ge 0,\n$$\n\nwe need to find the values of $x$ for which the parabola \n\n$$\ny=-{x}^{2}+3x\n$$\n\nlies *above* the $x$-axis or touches this axis.\n\nFirst, let's find the roots of the parabola:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-{x}^{2}+3x & =0 \\\\ -x(x-3) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the roots are $x=0$ and $x=3,$ and we can graph the parabola as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004892/assets/68d82c96c820a6a0bf5e3c74ea93cbf2091e96ebfa7dfe200e8beb140cb7962e.png)\n\nThe values marked in blue show all $x$-values where the parabola lies *above* the axis or touches the $x$-axis. \n\nSo, the solution to the inequality is $0\\le x\\le 3.$" 13194139534640 true] [17592186300496 1017 #edb/ref 17592186300497 13194139534640 true] [17592186300496 1089 "q-142177" 13194139534640 true] [17592186300496 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534640 true] [17592186300496 1100 "Find the solution of $-5{x}^{2}>10x.$" 13194139534640 true] [17592186300496 1113 #uuid "292302ac-904d-59fe-b02a-d8afa13eb915" 13194139534640 true] [17592186300496 1145 "To solve this inequality using the graphical method, we first need to move all of the numbers to the left-hand side so that the right-hand side is $0.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-5{x}^{2} & >10x \\\\ -5{x}^{2}-10x & >0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we want to find the values of $x$ for which the parabola $y=-5{x}^{2}-10x$ lies above the $x$-axis. Let's find the roots of the parabola by factoring:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-5{x}^{2}-10x & =0 \\\\ -5x(x+2) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe see that the roots are $x=0$ and $x=-2,$ and we can graph the parabola as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004892/assets/6cb044d4c6280d77dd525f6e2a8702d9fcba1553c2d33411407d69e09a6b715b.png)\n\nSince we are interested in solving \n\n$$\n-5{x}^{2}-10x>0,\n$$\n\nwe look for the part of the parabola that is above the $x$-axis. \n\nBased on the graph, the solution is $-2<x<0.$ \n\nUsing interval notation, we write $x\\in (-2,0).$" 13194139534640 true] [17592186300497 1000 #edb/ref 17592186300498 13194139534640 true] [17592186300497 1000 #edb/ref 17592186300499 13194139534640 true] [17592186300497 1000 #edb/ref 17592186300500 13194139534640 true] [17592186300497 1000 #edb/ref 17592186300501 13194139534640 true] [17592186300497 1000 #edb/ref 17592186300502 13194139534640 true] [17592186300497 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534640 true] [17592186300497 1041 "selection" 13194139534640 true] [17592186300497 1104 #edb/ref 17592186300501 13194139534640 true] [17592186300497 1110 #uuid "be4cc782-4666-5500-af79-b8103c59b4eb" 13194139534640 true] [17592186300498 1034 "x\\in (-\\infty ,-2)\\cup (2,\\infty )" 13194139534640 true] [17592186300498 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534640 true] [17592186300498 1111 #uuid "a5b86b07-5152-5bfa-a7dd-3b1b2394348e" 13194139534640 true] [17592186300499 1034 "x\\in (-\\infty ,0)\\cup (2,\\infty )" 13194139534640 true] [1759218