& =0 \\\\ -(x+3)(x-4) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe see that the roots are $x=-3$ and $x=4,$ and we can graph the parabola as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004892/assets/32e9a7babfbe9132a3a3e18c2f1efcbc3a33cd59bccc02099c7045b3fc39ee75.png)\n\nSince we are interested in solving \n\n$$\n-{x}^{2}+x+12>0,\n$$\n\n \nwe look for the part of the parabola that is **above** the $x$-axis. \n\nBased on the graph, the solution is $-3<x<4.$\n\nUsing interval notation, we write $x\\in (-3,4).$" 13194139534640 true] [17592186300561 1000 #edb/ref 17592186300562 13194139534640 true] [17592186300561 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534640 true] [17592186300561 1041 "field-1" 13194139534640 true] [17592186300561 1104 #edb/ref 17592186300562 13194139534640 true] [17592186300561 1110 #uuid "cf39dc5c-a856-5b78-a9f5-723f472e4485" 13194139534640 true] [17592186300562 1034 "-3" 13194139534640 true] [17592186300562 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534640 true] [17592186300562 1111 #uuid "2213bcde-f411-52e7-89d5-75c0d9453f8d" 13194139534640 true] [17592186300563 1000 #edb/ref 17592186300564 13194139534640 true] [17592186300563 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534640 true] [17592186300563 1041 "field-2" 13194139534640 true] [17592186300563 1104 #edb/ref 17592186300564 13194139534640 true] [17592186300563 1110 #uuid "1481635d-90cb-50f3-a54d-91682e323b61" 13194139534640 true] [17592186300564 1034 "4" 13194139534640 true] [17592186300564 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534640 true] [17592186300564 1111 #uuid "c57b760c-2f49-5596-b1a7-e36f9eb8cb8c" 13194139534640 true] [17592186300565 1017 #edb/ref 17592186300566 13194139534640 true] [17592186300565 1017 #edb/ref 17592186300569 13194139534640 true] [17592186300565 1089 "q-277671" 13194139534640 true] [17592186300565 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139534640 true] [17592186300565 1100 "Solve the inequality $-2{x}^{2}>10x+12$ and express the solution set in interval notation.\n\n$x\\in (${{field-1}}$,$\n{{field-2}}$)$" 13194139534640 true] [17592186300565 1113 #uuid "0f81b704-2a60-5224-96b8-0941c805eb95" 13194139534640 true] [17592186300565 1145 "To solve this inequality using the graphical method, we first need to move all of the terms to the left-hand side so that the right-hand side is $0.$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2{x}^{2} & >10x+12 \\\\ -2{x}^{2}-10x-12 & >0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we want to find the values of $x$ for which the parabola $y=-2{x}^{2}-10x-12$ lies **above** the $x$-axis. Let's find the roots of the parabola by factoring:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2{x}^{2}-10x-12 & =0 \\\\ 2{x}^{2}+10x+12 & =0 \\\\ (2{x}^{2}+6x)+(4x+12) & =0 \\\\ 2x(x+3)+4(x+3) & =0 \\\\ (2x+4)(x+3) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe see that the roots are $x=-3$ and $x=-2,$ and we can graph the parabola as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004892/assets/539e0e68f4a03c0bd4a309ebf2c4a00638d99c6eee233ca8f2cef3814e419c95.png)\n\nSince we are interested in solving \n\n$$\n-2{x}^{2}-10x-12>0,\n$$\n\n \nwe look for the part of the parabola that is **above** the $x$-axis.\n\nBased on the graph, the solution is $-3<x<-2.$\n\nUsing interval notation, we write $x\\in (-3,-2).$" 13194139534640 true] [17592186300566 1000 #edb/ref 17592186300567 13194139534640 true] [17592186300566 1000 #edb/ref 17592186300568 13194139534640 true] [17592186300566 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534640 true] [17592186300566 1041 "field-1" 13194139534640 true] [17592186300566 1104 #edb/ref 17592186300568 13194139534640 true] [17592186300566 1110 #uuid "472af46d-1570-5103-b2d3-1862fb2b88cd" 13194139534640 true] [17592186300567 1034 "3" 13194139534640 true] [17592186300567 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534640 true] [17592186300567 1111 #uuid "2c404b6a-96c5-5345-b717-148acadd2c70" 13194139534640 true] [17592186300568 1034 "-3" 13194139534640 true] [17592186300568 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534640 true] [17